1. She grew up in England. (Verbatim: "I grew up in England okay so you just you just gotta know that okay I grew up in England.")

2. She is half-Asian and has brothers, one of whom is named Papalia. (Verbatim: "I'm half, but even then, it's like, oh, but your brothers like spicy food, and even Papalia likes spicy food.")

3. She dislikes spicy food and considers herself sensitive to it. (Verbatim: "I don't even like slightly spicy foods, yet alone, like, adventurous activities.")

4. Her mother, Mama Elia, is disappointed in her for not liking spicy food and has called her a "disappointing Asian." (Verbatim: "Mama Elia is very, very, very, very, very disappointed in that fact, actually, um, and has stated several times that I am a, quote, disappointing Asian.")

5. She did not try Indian takeaway until after leaving her family home, as her father, Papa Elia, does not like it. (Verbatim: "I didn't actually get to try Indian takeaways until, until I left, until, until I left with my, my family home.")

6. She enjoys tikka masala and korma curries, but only if they are not spicy and have proper flavor. (Verbatim: "I do love a tikka masala, but it can't be spicy, a good tikka masala. I'm also quite fussy about my kormas.")

7. She dislikes the texture of nuts and was upset when her curry had many physical nuts in it. (Verbatim: "I don't like nuts I don't like their texture that's it like I don't I don't I don't like the texture of nuts okay I just don't.")

8. She dislikes finding bones in her food, especially in curry, and finds bone-in meat upsetting. (Verbatim: "I get so upset if there's like bone in my curry it it upsets me.")

9. She used to think all beef was chewy and unpleasant because her family always cooked it very well done, but later discovered properly cooked beef can be delicious. (Verbatim: "I thought all beef for the longest time was just this horrible chewy thing... and then I discovered that beef can actually be delicious.")

10. She appreciates well-cooked vegetables and dislikes traditionally boiled English vegetables that turn mushy. (Verbatim: "The traditional way to make english vegetables is to just boil it to an oblivion and it turns out if you like i don't know coat them in like honey and soy and roast them and it's just it could be delicious.") [end of text]



1. She has a memory of childhood blackberry picking during a visit from Australian relatives. (Verbatim: "i remember we went blackberry picking um we went to pick blackberries")
2. An Australian family member may have worked for Coca-Cola, which is why they brought a lot of Coca-Cola merchandise when visiting. (Verbatim: "i think it was something to do with like one of the family members in australia working for coca-cola or something")
3. She is face blind and cannot remember people's faces. (Verbatim: "i can't see faces i'm face blind so i can't remember what they look like")
4. She struggled with self-acceptance and does not currently like herself, but is trying. (Verbatim: "i don't like myself i'm trying okay and it's okay if you don't like yourself just trying to like yourself and is is um is good enough")
5. She used to work as a scientist before transitioning into computer science. (Verbatim: "for me i had to go from scientists to computers")
6. She finds it difficult to start new projects and often shifts focus before finishing. (Verbatim: "yes that is um that is that is definitely something i do a lot of")
7. She sets deadlines to help manage her tendency to abandon unfinished projects. (Verbatim: "my my only solution to that is setting myself deadlines to actually do it")
8. She grew up in an environment with competitive parents, which made starting new things difficult. (Verbatim: "if you're raised in an environment where you're constantly being compared or you have very competitive parents")
9. She believes learning should be enjoyed and not seen as a linear race against others. (Verbatim: "learning isn't linear... i picture it more like going to sea in the boats")
10. She finds it scary and difficult to change directions or start something new, but encourages trying anyway. (Verbatim: "literally getting that boat out to start with can be really tough and you might feel like it's not possible") [end of text]



1. She struggled with feeling disadvantaged compared to other computer science students and VTubers due to her different background. (Verbatim: "i didn't have the same advantages of what other computer science students would have... i don't have the same experience or skill set as a lot of other vtubers")

2. She once aspired to be a biologist focused on animal biology, possibly living in the jungle. (Verbatim: "when i say scientist i meant like biology like animal biology living in the jungle kind of thing")

3. She had a difficult school experience and was bullied, which motivated her through spite to maintain perfect attendance. (Verbatim: "i felt like if i gave up i'd i'd be letting those bullies win... i told myself out of complete spite i was gonna have 100 attendance and that i did get")

4. She has agoraphobia, which affects her when traveling and sometimes requires a full day of recovery indoors. (Verbatim: "i do my best to not let my agoraphobia get to me... i have to spend like just a whole day inside and just like mentally recover")

5. She describes herself as a shut-in and spent most of her childhood not traveling or going on holidays abroad. (Verbatim: "i'm quite the shut-in... my family never went on holiday abroad like growing up")

6. Her first trip abroad was to Asialand, which she paid for with her first full-time job, going with "mama elia". (Verbatim: "we never actually went to asialand until i paid for it with my first... full-time thing i was the first time and i saved money to go to asialand with mama elia")

7. She finds traveling to be a dream-like and deeply appreciative experience, feeling privileged to do so. (Verbatim: "there's some kind of like really special feeling to it feels like a dream for me when i travel")

8. She uses spite as a motivator in life, though acknowledges it shouldn't be a permanent source of fuel. (Verbatim: "spite is a great motivator i know it's the reason i'm still alive... as long as it's not your eternal fuel")

9. She is inspired by other VTubers' work rather than intimidated, despite initially feeling nervous about measuring up. (Verbatim: "it's incredible that i get to be friends with someone so amazing... it's not i think i think sometimes it can be quite easy to fall into seeing someone do really well and being like oh gosh")

10. She enjoys Coca-Cola and caffeine, referring to it as great and a source of fuel. (Verbatim: "caffeine's heckin great yes fuel me coca-cola heck yeah") [end of text]



1. She is from England and is accustomed to English culture. (Verbatim: "i think i get i'm quite used to english culture you know and like when i went to japan and then when i came back to england i was kind of like yay i can like you know talk on public transport and and i can i can um eat while walking and drink while walking")

2. She previously lived in or spent significant time in Japan, where she experienced the politeness of Japanese customer service. (Verbatim: "when i went to japan and then when i came back to england i was kind of like yay i can like you know talk on public transport")

3. She has a pet dog that she deeply misses when traveling. (Verbatim: "also my dog see my dog again i miss my dog when i travel i miss her tons i missed her so much")

4. She bought a white fluffy dog plushie from a crane machine in Japan as a substitute for her real dog while away. (Verbatim: "i bought a white fluffy dog stuff toy as a substitute while i was in japan i literally had it right here i have it right here um i got it from a i saw it in a in a crane machine and i couldn't resist it")

5. Her real dog is jealous of her plushie and reacts when she pets it. (Verbatim: "she keeps eating off the bed because she's jealous of it if i if i'm like petting it i'm like hell she like runs over and is like nope pick it up yeet love me instead")

6. She has never tried beef brisket and is both curious and slightly afraid of it due to its name sounding like "biscuit". (Verbatim: "i've never had brisket i don't know what brisket is i i don't know what it is it just sounds like biscuit and it scares me but i don't think it's a beef biscuit because that would be weird")

7. She is interested in trying American food, particularly intrigued by large portion sizes. (Verbatim: "i definitely want to try american food one day i've never i've i've i've heard so much about american food")

8. She plans to order kids' meals and large drinks if she ever visits an American McDonald's due to the large sizes. (Verbatim: "i think i'll get kids meals there if i ever go there because like i don't think i could eat it all i want to i want to get one of those giant cups i hear that like the cup size is massive like i want a giant cup of of of cola")

9. She visited Kinosaki, an onsen town in Japan, and highly recommends it for its multiple hot springs and anime mascot. (Verbatim: "i really if you want something slightly different um i absolutely adored going to um kinosaki um but it's quite difficult to get to like it's quite far but that was it's like an onsen town and it's so nice")

10. She owns an acrylic standee of the Kinosaki anime mascot, which she finds very cute. (Verbatim: "i actually have my acrylic standee of the kinosaki anime girl mascot yeah wait let me grab her she's up here she's so she's so she's so cute") [end of text]



1. She climbed Mount Fuji and reached the summit. (Verbatim: "i climbed mount fuji i claimed it i climbed all the way to the top")  
2. She has a talent for moving her eyebrows independently, which she trained deliberately. (Verbatim: "i can move my eyebrows individually... i had to like train and build up the muscles in my eyebrows")  
3. She finds it difficult to deal with pressure from others' expectations, especially after initially excelling at things. (Verbatim: "i am usually someone that would be like i think it's really difficult in that situation because... you have the expectations of people around you")  
4. She used to take a full day off work specifically to unpack when moving apartments. (Verbatim: "when i moved before i remember i used to take a day of work just to just to unpack")  
5. She left her apartment in a state of unpacked boxes for a couple of weeks after moving in. (Verbatim: "it lasted a couple of weeks yeah... it took a while for me to even unpack my suitcase")  
6. Her work style is all-or-nothing—she avoids tasks until suddenly doing them all at once. (Verbatim: "i am a zero or 100 kind of worker... one day i'll wake up and be like i'm done living in this mess and then just just hard unpack the whole day")  
7. She believes admitting failure and trying anyway is more impressive than natural talent. (Verbatim: "what is truly impressive... is someone trying and admitting they can't do something and being willing to work on it")  
8. She once had a 20-game losing streak in League of Legends, including placements, and was placed in Silver. (Verbatim: "i think my longest lost streak was 20 games in a row... that head game was painful i had to climb out of there")  
9. Her favorite pizza flavor is pineapple. (Verbatim: "i really like pineapple")  
10. She dislikes pizzas with multiple types of meat combined, such as meat feast. (Verbatim: "i don't like having different types of meat together like when i see like pizzas that are like meat feast and stuff") [end of text]



